PATCH: zephyr_tls_session_export — cross-sleep TLS session persistence
=======================================================================

Written against: Zephyr 4.3.0  (git tag v4.3.0, commit prefix 7bad851 / 2ccca60)
Target platform: ESP32-S3 N16R8 on Zephyr RTOS with mbedTLS builtin
Application:     /workspace/projects/hello_eink  (LLSS e-ink client, deep-sleep loop)

SUMMARY
-------
Zephyr's TLS socket implementation keeps `struct tls_context` private to
`sockets_tls.c`.  There is no public API to extract or inject a serialised
mbedTLS session, so a resumed handshake after deep sleep (where DRAM is lost
but RTC slow RAM survives) is impossible without this patch.

The patch adds two new TLS socket options:

  TLS_SESSION_EXPORT  (21)  — getsockopt after a successful connect.
      Serialises the negotiated session via `mbedtls_ssl_session_save()` into
      a caller-supplied buffer.  The application stores this buffer in RTC
      slow RAM (section `.rtc_noinit`, survives deep sleep) tagged with a
      magic sentinel so it can be distinguished from uninitialised RAM.

  TLS_SESSION_IMPORT  (22)  — setsockopt before the next connect.
      Copies the raw bytes into a heap buffer owned by the TLS context.
      `tls_session_restore()` uses these bytes as a fallback when the
      in-memory client-session cache (which is cleared on every reboot) has
      no entry for the peer.

The option numbers 21 and 22 are chosen to follow the highest existing
option in socket.h at the time of writing (TLS_CERT_VERIFY_CALLBACK = 20).
If upstream Zephyr adds new options that collide, renumber and update
TLS_SESSION_EXPORT / TLS_SESSION_IMPORT in both socket.h and llss_client.c.

DESIGN CONSTRAINTS (read before porting)
-----------------------------------------
1. `struct tls_context` is defined entirely inside sockets_tls.c and is never
   exposed in a header.  The two new fields `ext_session` (uint8_t *) and
   `ext_session_len` (size_t) are appended at the END of the anonymous
   `options` sub-struct so that all existing field offsets are preserved.
   If the upstream struct gains new option fields after the patch is applied
   the patch hunk for the struct may conflict — resolve by keeping
   `ext_session` / `ext_session_len` as the last two members of `options`.

2. The `options` sub-struct closing brace `} options;` is the most fragile
   part of this patch.  Any upstream addition of a new option field will
   appear immediately before that brace and will cause a conflict.  Resolution:
   keep the two ext_session fields as the last members, move the hunk context
   lines to wherever the new upstream fields were inserted.

3. `tls_session_restore()` is called inside `tls_perform_handshake()` just
   before `mbedtls_ssl_handshake()`.  The fallback branch added by this patch
   executes only when `tls_session_get()` returns non-zero (cache miss).
   If the Zephyr maintainers ever restructure that call site, ensure the
   fallback is still invoked at the same point in the handshake flow.

4. The session serialisation format is version-specific mbedTLS wire encoding.
   If the mbedTLS bundled version changes (check MBEDTLS_VERSION_STRING in
   /opt/toolchains/zephyr/modules/crypto/mbedtls/include/mbedtls/version.h)
   the application must invalidate any stored RTC session (e.g. change
   LLSS_TLS_SESSION_MAGIC in llss_client.c) so stale bytes from a previous
   mbedTLS version are never fed to `mbedtls_ssl_session_load()`.

5. `mbedtls_ssl_get_session()` copies the session; the copy is freed in
   `tls_opt_session_export_get()` with `mbedtls_ssl_session_free()`.  The
   original session inside `mbedtls_ssl_context` is unaffected.

6. The heap buffer in `ctx->options.ext_session` is allocated with
   `mbedtls_calloc` and freed unconditionally in `tls_release()`.  If
   `tls_release` is ever refactored ensure this free is not orphaned.

BEFORE PORTING — CHECK IF THE FEATURE IS NOW UPSTREAM
--------------------------------------------------------
Before spending any effort adapting this patch to a new Zephyr version, verify
that the functionality has not already been added by the Zephyr maintainers.
Run the checks below against the new Zephyr tree.  If ALL pass, discard this
patch entirely and update llss_client.c to use the upstream API instead.

1. Socket option defines already present?
     grep -n "TLS_SESSION_EXPORT\|TLS_SESSION_IMPORT" \
         include/zephyr/net/socket.h
   Expected when upstream: two matching #define lines.
   If found: note the option numbers, ensure llss_client.c uses them.

2. getsockopt/setsockopt dispatch cases wired?
     grep -n "TLS_SESSION_EXPORT\|TLS_SESSION_IMPORT" \
         subsys/net/lib/sockets/sockets_tls.c
   Expected when upstream: at least one match in ztls_getsockopt_ctx and one
   in ztls_setsockopt_ctx.

3. Session serialisation API available to the socket layer?
     grep -n "mbedtls_ssl_session_save\|mbedtls_ssl_session_load" \
         subsys/net/lib/sockets/sockets_tls.c
   Expected when upstream: calls present (they may be wrapped differently).

4. Check the Zephyr changelog / git log for related commits:
     git log --oneline --all --grep="session.*export\|session.*import\|TLS_SESSION" \
         -- subsys/net/lib/sockets/sockets_tls.c include/zephyr/net/socket.h
   Any hit that mentions session export/import/serialise is a strong signal
   the feature landed upstream.

5. Check upstream issue / PR tracker:
   Search https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/issues for
   "TLS session export" or "TLS session resume RTC".  A merged PR means
   the feature is in the tree; use the upstream API number instead of 21/22.

If NONE of the above find anything, the feature is still absent upstream and
this patch must be ported.  Proceed to the hunk-by-hunk guide below.

HUNK-BY-HUNK GUIDE FOR PORTING
--------------------------------

Hunk 1 — include/zephyr/net/socket.h  (@@ -262 @@)
  Context line: `#define TLS_CERT_VERIFY_CALLBACK 20`
  Action: two new #define lines inserted after it.
  Risk: LOW.  Only conflict if upstream adds a new option with value 21 or 22.
  Fix: renumber to the next free values and update llss_client.c.

Hunk 2 — sockets_tls.c  (@@ -211 @@)  — tls_context.options struct
  Context lines: the `cert_verify` member inside the options struct.
  Action: two new fields appended before `} options;`.
  Risk: MEDIUM.  Any new upstream option field added here will conflict.
  Fix: keep ext_session / ext_session_len as the last two members before
  `} options;` regardless of where upstream adds its new field.

Hunk 3 — sockets_tls.c  (@@ -546 @@)  — tls_release()
  Context lines: `mbedtls_pk_free` ... `tls->is_used = false`.
  Action: free ext_session before marking context unused.
  Risk: LOW.  Only conflicts if tls_release() body is restructured.

Hunk 4 — sockets_tls.c  (@@ -575 @@)  — new functions after peer_addr_cmp()
  Context line: closing `}` of peer_addr_cmp, then `tls_session_save`.
  Action: inserts tls_opt_session_export_get() and tls_opt_session_import_set().
  Risk: LOW.  Free-standing new functions; no dependency on surrounding code
  except the mbedtls_ssl_session_save/load/get/free API.

Hunk 5 — sockets_tls.c  (@@ -713 @@)  — tls_session_restore() fallback
  Context lines: `tls_session_get()` failure branch ("Session not found").
  Action: replaces the simple "goto exit" with an ext_session fallback.
  Risk: MEDIUM.  If tls_session_restore() is refactored (e.g. the get/set
  split is reorganised) re-check that the fallback still runs before
  `mbedtls_ssl_set_session()` and after `tls_session_get()` fails.

Hunk 6 — sockets_tls.c  (@@ -3712 @@)  — ztls_getsockopt_ctx dispatch
  Context line: `case TLS_SESSION_CACHE:` block just before `TLS_CERT_VERIFY_RESULT`.
  Action: new `case TLS_SESSION_EXPORT:` inserted.
  Risk: LOW.  Only conflicts if the surrounding switch cases are reordered.

Hunk 7 — sockets_tls.c  (@@ -3838 @@)  — ztls_setsockopt_ctx dispatch
  Context line: `case TLS_SESSION_CACHE_PURGE:` block just before `TLS_CERT_VERIFY_CALLBACK`.
  Action: new `case TLS_SESSION_IMPORT:` inserted.
  Risk: LOW.  Same as Hunk 6.

RELATED FILES (not part of this patch, but must be consistent with it)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  /workspace/projects/hello_eink/src/llss_client.c
      - Uses TLS_SESSION_EXPORT / TLS_SESSION_IMPORT socket options.
      - Declares rtc_tls_session_buf, rtc_tls_session_len, rtc_tls_session_magic
        with __attribute__((section(".rtc_noinit"))) so they survive deep sleep.
      - LLSS_TLS_SESSION_MAGIC sentinel: change if mbedTLS version changes.
      - LLSS_TLS_SESSION_BUF_SIZE (512 B): increase if mbedtls_ssl_session_save
        returns -ENOBUFS (TLS 1.3 tickets can be larger than TLS 1.2 sessions).
  /workspace/projects/hello_eink/prj.conf
      - CONFIG_MBEDTLS_SSL_SESSION_TICKETS=y  (required for TLS 1.3 resumption)
      - CONFIG_NET_SOCKETS_TLS_MAX_CLIENT_SESSION_COUNT=1  (in-memory cache)
      - CONFIG_MBEDTLS_SSL_PROTO_TLS1_3=y  (enables ticket-based resumption)

---

diff --git a/include/zephyr/net/socket.h b/include/zephyr/net/socket.h
index 7bad851f238..b65df20d398 100644
--- a/include/zephyr/net/socket.h
+++ b/include/zephyr/net/socket.h
@@ -262,6 +262,28 @@ extern "C" {
  */
 #define TLS_CERT_VERIFY_CALLBACK 20
 
+/** @brief Export the serialized TLS session after a successful handshake.
+ *
+ *  getsockopt() with this option fills the caller's buffer with the raw
+ *  mbedTLS session bytes (same format as mbedtls_ssl_session_save()).
+ *  The returned @p optlen is the actual number of bytes written.
+ *  Returns -ENOBUFS if the buffer is too small (optlen is updated to the
+ *  required size) or -ENOENT if no session is available yet.
+ *  Use after zsock_connect() succeeds to snapshot the session for storage
+ *  in RTC RAM / NVS to survive deep sleep (Phase B.2).
+ */
+#define TLS_SESSION_EXPORT 21
+
+/** @brief Import a previously exported TLS session before connecting.
+ *
+ *  setsockopt() with this option loads the raw mbedTLS session bytes
+ *  (same format as mbedtls_ssl_session_load()) into the TLS context so
+ *  that the next zsock_connect() can attempt an abbreviated handshake.
+ *  Must be called after @ref TLS_SESSION_CACHE is enabled and before
+ *  zsock_connect().  Pass optval=NULL / optlen=0 to clear.
+ */
+#define TLS_SESSION_IMPORT 22
+
 /* Valid values for @ref TLS_PEER_VERIFY option */
 #define TLS_PEER_VERIFY_NONE 0     /**< Peer verification disabled. */
 #define TLS_PEER_VERIFY_OPTIONAL 1 /**< Peer verification optional. */
diff --git a/subsys/net/lib/sockets/sockets_tls.c b/subsys/net/lib/sockets/sockets_tls.c
index 2ccca60a34d..6e35826e475 100644
--- a/subsys/net/lib/sockets/sockets_tls.c
+++ b/subsys/net/lib/sockets/sockets_tls.c
@@ -211,7 +211,15 @@ __net_socket struct tls_context {
 #if defined(CONFIG_NET_SOCKETS_TLS_CERT_VERIFY_CALLBACK)
 		struct tls_cert_verify_cb cert_verify;
 #endif /* CONFIG_NET_SOCKETS_TLS_CERT_VERIFY_CALLBACK */
-	} options;
+
+                /** Externally supplied session bytes for cross-sleep
+                 *  resumption (TLS_SESSION_IMPORT / Phase B.2).  Loaded
+                 *  into the ssl context by tls_session_restore() when the
+                 *  in-memory client_cache has no entry for the peer.
+                 */
+                uint8_t *ext_session;
+                size_t ext_session_len;
+        } options;
 
 #if defined(CONFIG_NET_SOCKETS_ENABLE_DTLS)
 	/** Context information for DTLS timing. */
@@ -546,13 +554,19 @@ static int tls_release(struct tls_context *tls)
 	mbedtls_pk_free(&tls->priv_key);
 #endif
 
-	tls->is_used = false;
+        if (tls->options.ext_session != NULL) {
+                mbedtls_free(tls->options.ext_session);
+                tls->options.ext_session = NULL;
+                tls->options.ext_session_len = 0;
+        }
 
-	return 0;
+        tls->is_used = false;
+
+        return 0;
 }
 
 static bool peer_addr_cmp(const struct sockaddr *addr,
-			  const struct sockaddr *peer_addr)
+                          const struct sockaddr *peer_addr)
 {
 	if (addr->sa_family != peer_addr->sa_family) {
 		return false;
@@ -575,6 +589,77 @@ static bool peer_addr_cmp(const struct sockaddr *addr,
 	return false;
 }
 
+/* Phase B.2: export the active TLS session into a caller-supplied buffer.
+ * Called from ztls_getsockopt_ctx via TLS_SESSION_EXPORT.
+ * The buffer format is mbedtls_ssl_session_save() wire encoding, suitable
+ * for storing in RTC RAM and later restoring via TLS_SESSION_IMPORT. */
+static int tls_opt_session_export_get(struct tls_context *ctx,
+				      void *optval, socklen_t *optlen)
+{
+	mbedtls_ssl_session session;
+	size_t session_len;
+	int ret;
+
+	mbedtls_ssl_session_init(&session);
+
+	ret = mbedtls_ssl_get_session(&ctx->ssl, &session);
+	if (ret != 0) {
+		mbedtls_ssl_session_free(&session);
+		return -ENOENT;
+	}
+
+	/* Probe for required size */
+	(void)mbedtls_ssl_session_save(&session, NULL, 0, &session_len);
+
+	if ((size_t)*optlen < session_len) {
+		mbedtls_ssl_session_free(&session);
+		*optlen = (socklen_t)session_len;
+		return -ENOBUFS;
+	}
+
+	ret = mbedtls_ssl_session_save(&session, optval, *optlen, &session_len);
+	mbedtls_ssl_session_free(&session);
+
+	if (ret != 0) {
+		return -EIO;
+	}
+
+	*optlen = (socklen_t)session_len;
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/* Phase B.2: store externally supplied session bytes in the TLS context so
+ * that tls_session_restore() can attempt an abbreviated handshake even after
+ * a reboot (RTC RAM path).  The bytes are a copy owned by this context and
+ * freed in tls_release(). */
+static int tls_opt_session_import_set(struct tls_context *ctx,
+				      const void *optval, socklen_t optlen)
+{
+	if (optval == NULL || optlen == 0) {
+		if (ctx->options.ext_session != NULL) {
+			mbedtls_free(ctx->options.ext_session);
+			ctx->options.ext_session = NULL;
+			ctx->options.ext_session_len = 0;
+		}
+		return 0;
+	}
+
+	uint8_t *buf = mbedtls_calloc(1, optlen);
+
+	if (buf == NULL) {
+		return -ENOMEM;
+	}
+
+	if (ctx->options.ext_session != NULL) {
+		mbedtls_free(ctx->options.ext_session);
+	}
+
+	memcpy(buf, optval, optlen);
+	ctx->options.ext_session = buf;
+	ctx->options.ext_session_len = optlen;
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int tls_session_save(const struct sockaddr *peer_addr,
 			    mbedtls_ssl_session *session)
 {
@@ -713,8 +798,25 @@ static void tls_session_restore(struct tls_context *context,
 
 	ret = tls_session_get(&peer_addr, &session);
 	if (ret < 0) {
-		NET_DBG("Session not found for %p", context);
-		goto exit;
+		/* In-memory cache miss — fall back to externally supplied
+		 * session bytes (TLS_SESSION_IMPORT, e.g. from RTC RAM). */
+		if (context->options.ext_session != NULL &&
+		    context->options.ext_session_len > 0) {
+			ret = mbedtls_ssl_session_load(
+				&session,
+				context->options.ext_session,
+				context->options.ext_session_len);
+			if (ret != 0) {
+				NET_DBG("Ext session load failed %p: -0x%x",
+					context, -ret);
+				goto exit;
+			}
+			NET_DBG("TLS: restoring session from ext buffer (%p)",
+				context);
+		} else {
+			NET_DBG("Session not found for %p", context);
+			goto exit;
+		}
 	}
 
 	ret = mbedtls_ssl_set_session(&context->ssl, &session);
@@ -3712,6 +3814,10 @@ int ztls_getsockopt_ctx(struct tls_context *ctx, int level, int optname,
 		err = tls_opt_session_cache_get(ctx, optval, optlen);
 		break;
 
+	case TLS_SESSION_EXPORT:
+		err = tls_opt_session_export_get(ctx, optval, optlen);
+		break;
+
 	case TLS_CERT_VERIFY_RESULT:
 		err = tls_opt_cert_verify_result_get(ctx, optval, optlen);
 		break;
@@ -3838,6 +3944,10 @@ int ztls_setsockopt_ctx(struct tls_context *ctx, int level, int optname,
 		err = tls_opt_session_cache_purge_set(ctx, optval, optlen);
 		break;
 
+	case TLS_SESSION_IMPORT:
+		err = tls_opt_session_import_set(ctx, optval, optlen);
+		break;
+
 	case TLS_CERT_VERIFY_CALLBACK:
 		err = tls_opt_cert_verify_callback_set(ctx, optval, optlen);
 		break;
